cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use InferBench in your research or benchmarks, please cite it as below."
title: "InferBench: measured benchmarking of local LLM inference engines"
abstract: >-
  InferBench is a cross-platform desktop application that downloads, launches and
  benchmarks local LLM inference engines (llama.cpp and friends) and cloud APIs from
  a single click. It detects the host hardware, picks a working configuration per
  model and quantization, and measures time-to-first-token, tokens per second, VRAM
  usage and answer quality on real runs — no synthetic or extrapolated numbers. It
  also exposes the orchestrated models over a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server,
  covering text and local image generation. Everything runs on the user's machine.
type: software
